  "equipment_type": "Power meter (power quality analyser)",
  "applies_to": "KMB systems panel and DIN-rail meters and analysers with firmware 4.x, per 'Modbus-TCP and Modbus-RTU protocol documentation' (revision of January 19, 2023). Which blocks a model supports depends on the instrument and its firmware modules.",
  "summary": "KMB systems (Czech Republic) builds the SMC, SMY, SMZ, SML, PA and ARTIQ families of power meters and power-quality analysers. Firmware 4.x devices share one Modbus register map over RS-485 (Modbus RTU, auto-detected alongside KMB's own protocol) or Ethernet (Modbus TCP, port 502). This map covers the compact 19000-19121 block of the most-used values as IEEE floats with units, power factor, status and identification.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "Addresses are printed in decimal and hex as PDU (wire) addresses. The manual's modpoll examples use the -0 switch ('Modbus PDU addressing') with -r 528 for the device number and -r 4352 for the voltages, and a footnote says that without -0 every address would need +1."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "4.x (document lists FW compatibility up to 4.x releases)",
  "source": {
    "title": "Modbus-TCP and Modbus-RTU protocol documentation for panel meters, power quality analyzers and power factor controllers",
    "doc_number": "Modbus manual v4.0 EN rev 1.8",
    "revision_date": "2023-01-19",
    "url": "https://kmb.cz/en/download/download-documents/4-application-notes?download=200:modbus-manual-v4-0-en",
    "pages": "Communication options p. 1; functions, encoding, addressing, examples pp. 2-4; device identification p. 8; actual data pp. 17-21; 19000 block pp. 32-33"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Encoding (2.3): multi-byte values are big-endian and 32/64-bit values run MSB to LSB across consecutive registers, so floats are ABCD. The modpoll example reads voltages around 236 V as big-endian floats.",
    "Function 04 (input registers) returns actual 200 ms values; function 03 (holding registers) on the same addresses returns the averaged values set up in the instrument. Registers are listed here as input registers.",
    "Left out: the energy rows of the 19000 block (19054-19108). Their unit column says Wh / VAh / varh while the block's introduction says the registers give total kWh/kvarh counts, so the unit is ambiguous. The 0x2000 energy block (64-bit doubles) has no unit stated, so it is left out as well.",
    "Left out: the device number (528, printed only as '32b' with no signed/unsigned type), the detailed actual-data blocks 0x1100-0x13xx (no units printed), harmonics, archives, aggregated min/max blocks, RCM, PQ and NOVAR power-factor-controller registers, and the configuration/reset blocks.",
    "Multi-feeder instruments use the device address for feeder 1 and mirror the map for feeders 2-12 at address (X-1) x 20 + base address; their base address is limited to 1-20.",
    "Over RS-485 the device recognises Modbus RTU and KMB's own protocol automatically. The manual says KMB devices default to no parity; device address and baud must be set per the user manual."
  ],
